{"guide":{"questionsToConsider":["Do you want feedback on the product as a whole, or on one feature or flow?","Should you send it after a specific action, so the task question has a clear answer?","Who will reply to the people who agree to a follow-up, and how soon?","Which qualities in the grid do you actually have the power to change?"],"howToUseResponses":"Read the answers from people who gave up first, grouped by where it broke, because each one is a task your product failed at. Then set the scores next to their reasons: a 3 with a complaint about speed is a different fix from a 3 about missing features. Watch the share of users who'd be very disappointed without you over time, and follow up with volunteers while the problem is still fresh in their minds.","customizeSteps":["Replace \"our product\" in the greeting with your product's name, and narrow the task question if you're studying one feature.","Rename the grid rows to the qualities your users care about most.","Trigger the link after users complete or abandon a key task, or share it in your product's help menu."],"faqs":[{"q":"What questions should a user satisfaction survey ask?","a":"What the person was trying to do, whether they managed it, an overall score and the reason for it, and what to improve next. Tying the score to a real task makes it far easier to act on."},{"q":"What is the difference between user satisfaction and NPS?","a":"Satisfaction asks how well the product works for someone, while NPS asks whether they'd recommend it. This template focuses on satisfaction and the reason behind it; you can add an NPS question if you track both."},{"q":"How often should I run a user satisfaction survey?","a":"Send it after meaningful tasks rather than on a fixed schedule, and avoid asking the same person more than once every few months."},{"q":"Can I send different questions to people who had a bad experience?","a":"Yes. This template already does: people who struggled or gave up get their own follow-ups, and you can edit the branching in the builder."}]},"doc":{"schemaVersion":9,"title":"User satisfaction survey","description":"Learn how well your product works for the people using it, and the reason behind each score.","blocks":[{"id":"blk_usersati00","ref":"welcome","title":"We'd like to know how using our product is going for you. Five minutes at most, and your answers go straight to the team building it.","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"buttonLabel":"Start","type":"welcome"},{"id":"blk_usersati01","ref":"task","title":"The last time you used it, what were you trying to get done?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"long_text","minLength":0,"maxLength":500,"aiQualityCheck":false},{"id":"blk_usersati02","ref":"completed","title":"Did you manage it?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_yes_easily","label":"Yes, easily","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_yes_but_it","label":"Yes, but it took some effort","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_no","label":"No","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_usersati03","ref":"hard_part","title":"What made it harder than it should have been?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"long_text","minLength":0,"maxLength":800,"aiQualityCheck":false},{"id":"blk_usersati04","ref":"where_broke","title":"Where did it go wrong?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":{"askStyle":"Ask for the step they were on and what they saw, not their opinion of the product.","examples":[]},"media":null,"type":"long_text","minLength":0,"maxLength":800,"aiQualityCheck":false},{"id":"blk_usersati05","ref":"instead","title":"What did you do instead?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_tried_again_later","label":"Tried again later","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_asked_for_help","label":"Asked for help","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_used_a_different","label":"Used a different tool","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_gave_up_on","label":"Gave up on it for now","image_key":null}],"allowOther":true},{"id":"blk_usersati06","ref":"satisfaction","title":"Overall, how satisfied are you with it?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"rating","scale":5,"shape":"star"},{"id":"blk_usersati07","ref":"reason","title":"What's the main reason for that score?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"long_text","minLength":0,"maxLength":800,"aiQualityCheck":false},{"id":"blk_usersati08","ref":"qualities","title":"How would you rate each of these?","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"matrix","rows":[{"id":"opt_row_speed","label":"Speed"},{"id":"opt_row_reliability","label":"Reliability"},{"id":"opt_row_finding_what","label":"Finding what you need"},{"id":"opt_row_how_it","label":"How it looks and feels"},{"id":"opt_row_help_when","label":"Help when you're stuck"}],"columns":[{"id":"opt_col_poor","label":"Poor"},{"id":"opt_col_fair","label":"Fair"},{"id":"opt_col_good","label":"Good"},{"id":"opt_col_excellent","label":"Excellent"}],"multiplePerRow":false},{"id":"blk_usersati09","ref":"frequency","title":"How often do you use it?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_every_day","label":"Every day","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_a_few_times","label":"A few times a week","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_a_few_times_2","label":"A few times a month","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_less_often","label":"Less often","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_usersati10","ref":"without_it","title":"How would you feel if you could no longer use it?","requi